   Well, I finally got my system to cooperate again, and here's the
rest of the patch.

http://www.contrib.andrew.cmu.edu/~ajo/free-software/nethack/unidring343.diff

This patch does the following things (where "emerald" and "jade" are
understood to stand in for any old gemstones, as appropriate):

  1. If you haven't identified emerald yet, emerald rings will appear
as "green stone rings" in your inventory.
  2. Also, they'll appear as "ring of levitation (green stone)" in
the '\' discovery screen, until emerald is identified.
  3. Identifying a ring with ?oID will also identify its gemstone;
thus, identifying a ring of levitation will also identify emeralds.
  4. Wishing for "a green stone ring" will give you an emerald or jade
ring at random.
  5. Rings in the player's starting inventory are fully identified,
including the gemstone.

My comments:
  3. This makes the identification of gems much easier.
  4. This is obviously the Right Thing. However, a little wizmode testing
seems to show that wishing for "a green stone" or "a green gem" always
gets you an emerald. Is this true? If so, why?
  5. This makes the identification of gems much easier for wizards in
particular, and gives them a good chance of making lots of $$$ in the
Gnomish Mines (if they start out with a diamond ring, say).

   So, as I said back when this thread was still active, I'm not a fan
of this YANI; I think it's unbalancing and not-common-sensical; but it
was a fun patch to make.

